  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manager Indore Depot Britannia ... vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh Health ... on 27 November, 2024 Author: Milind Ramesh Phadke Bench: Milind Ramesh Phadke 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At G Wa L I O R Before Hon'Ble Shri Justice Milind Ramesh Phadke On The 27th Of November, 2024 Writ Petition No. 2667 of 2015 (Manager, Indore Depot, Britannia Industries Limited Vs State Of Madhya Pradesh & Ors.) Appearance: (By Shri Rajesh Batre- Advocate With Shri Vishal Tripathi - Adovcate For Petitioners) (By Shri B.M. Patel - Government Advocate For Respondent/State. ------------------------------------------------------------- Order The instant writ petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India has been filed by the petitioners challenging the legality and validity of the complaint filed by the respondent No.4 and the consequent proceedings against the petitioners by the respondent No.2 after the sanction order dated 20.02.2015 for filing complaint against the petitioners thereby informing the petitioners that cognizance of the complaint filed by the respondent No.4 has been taken against them and directing the petitioner to appear and show cause as to why they ought not be punished under Section 52 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 for alleged contravention of Section 26 and 27 of Food Safety and Standards Act.",
    "facts": "",
